      {
        "id": 12553,
        "name": "Gislef",
        "username": "Gislef",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/4af34b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-04T22:40:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We're a bit confused by this card. And we couldn't find anything about it here. (Pardons if we missed it.)</p><p>It says, \"If a Proletariat would take 2 or more damage, remove <strong>that </strong>Proletariat from the map instead.\"</p><p>Which Proletariat is \"that\" Proletariat?</p><p>So instead of Pro taking two damage, he essentially takes all of his damage and is removed from the map. We're not sure what that accomlishes.</p><p>We get the impression that the removal is supposed to negate the 2+ damage. Spiff's FAQ, page 8, \"But if he were to decide not to block one of the attack dice, he <em>could choose to lose a clone instead and take no damage</em>.\" But that doesn't seem to be what the card says. It says \"<strong>that </strong>Proletariat\" (the clone takng the damage) is removed.</p><p>If it said \"remove <strong>a </strong>Proletariat...\" the FAQ would make sense. But \"that\" Proletariat seems to be pretty specific to the one taking damage.</p><p>What are we missing? :( Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:07.866Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 2,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 10.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 12551,
        "topic_slug": "proletariats-defensive-sacrifice",
        "display_username": "Gislef",
        "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_name": "playtesters",
        "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
        "flair_bg_color": "",
        "flair_color": "",
        "flair_group_id": 41,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
