        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": true,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>We&#39;re a bit confused by this card. And we couldn&#39;t find anything about it here. (Pardons if we missed it.)</p><p>It says, &quot;If a Proletariat would take 2 or more damage, remove <strong>that </strong>Proletariat from the map instead.&quot;</p><p>Which Proletariat is &quot;that&quot; Proletariat?</p><p>So instead of Pro taking two damage, he essentially takes all of his damage and is removed from the map. We&#39;re not sure what that accomlishes.</p><p>We get the impression that the removal is supposed to negate the 2+ damage. Spiff&#39;s FAQ, page 8, &quot;But if he were to decide not to block one of the attack dice, he <em>could choose to lose a clone instead and take no damage</em>.&quot; But that doesn&#39;t seem to be what the card says. It says &quot;<strong>that </strong>Proletariat&quot; (the clone takng the damage) is removed.</p><p>If it said &quot;remove <strong>a </strong>Proletariat...&quot; the FAQ would make sense. But &quot;that&quot; Proletariat seems to be pretty specific to the one taking damage.</p><p>What are we missing? :( Thanks!</p>",
        "actions_summary": [],
